"""
MHE performance-regression cases: collective key generation, local CKKS (Lattiseq) operations, collective
decryption/bootstrapping, MPC<->MHE switching, Ciphertensor operations and matmul variants, the multiparty types
(MPP/MPA/MPU) and MHE end-to-end workloads.

Run with --skip-mhe-setup: the binary calls mpc.mhe.default_setup() itself, inside the timed case mhe.setup.keygen
(always run and reported, since every other case needs the keys).

    sequre build -release tests/bench/bench_mhe.codon -o bench_mhe
    LD_PRELOAD=$HOME/.sequre/lib/sequre_align64.so ./bench_mhe --local --skip-mhe-setup [--cases=...] [--out=DIR]
    ./bench_mhe --list

Without the alignment shim, HE code segfaults on AVX hosts. See tests/bench/harness.codon for the output
format and scripts/bench.sh for the workflow.
"""
